The crystal acts as an evolving, spreading threat (like living enemy waves). It spreads across the world, absorbs elements to grow stronger, and eventually sends enemies toward the player. The player has limited map space and travel time, so efficient routing between building, exploring, and powering up is key.
Gameplay splits into two phases:

Maze / Strategy Phase (longer): Build walls, dig, grow vegetation, channel rivers, explore ruins, manage crystal spread, and do light RPG activities.
Fighting Phase (shorter, action-focused): Direct combat with weapons, armor, and relics once the crystal is strong enough or the player pushes back.

Win Condition: Destroy all crystal spawn points (original spawn has a boss; others have minibosses).
Strict Map Generation Rules

Exactly 5 interior biomes per map (plains, steppe, forest, marsh, highland — one instance each). Ocean and mountain borders are separate edge features.
Ocean edge: flat with proper integrated shoreline.
Mountain edge: very tall and effectively unclimbable (ramps/diagonal pieces stop after a height cutoff).
Ramps and diagonal pieces use frequency variables (not every height change gets one).
World generation must remain fully functional with arbitrary voxel scale changes.

Key Mechanics

Crystal System: Simplified pressure-based fluid simulation. Slowed by vegetation/rivers, cannot absorb water (only builds over it). Absorbs plants/animals/ruins to gain power and unlock new enemy spawns/behaviors. Forests act as natural barriers.
Player Tools: Build walls (block/redirect crystal), dig (deeper = slower), plant vegetation (area denial), channel rivers, explore ruins/artifacts (extra crystal spawn points with rewards/risks).
Strategic Choices: Let crystal absorb towns/farms for evolution (unlocks stronger enemies) or defend them? Kill passive mobs or let them feed the crystal?
Progression: Stats, relics, weapons/armor. Crystal absorption drives enemy variety (e.g., farm absorption → suicide-bomber animals).
Enemies: Crystal-type (evolving) + fantasy RPG mobs. Passive world animals.

Requirements for All Systems
Highly data-driven and modular (Resources, GameConfig, JSON export/import). Clean separation with strong integration points (crystal ↔ terrain ↔ building ↔ entities ↔ stats). Performance-conscious for chunked voxels. Easy to extend (new biomes, relics, enemy types, etc.).

