## Root causes

### 1. Boot deadlock (visuals never populated)
`VoxelWorld._ready` awaits `world_features.ensure_ready()`, which awaited `GameVisualRegistry.ensure_ready()`, which waited for `ChunkManager` — but `ChunkManager` is only created **after** `world_features` finishes. Terrain never streamed; sprites/billboards had no heightfield to anchor to.

### 2. Double-free on teardown
Chunk views were `queue_free()`'d without `remove_child()` during streaming/rebuild. Inflight mesh tasks and the completion queue could still touch freed `MultiMeshInstance3D` nodes during Godot shutdown (especially with perf presets re-applying twice on boot).

---

## Fixes applied

| Area | Change |
|------|--------|
| **GameVisualRegistry** | Split `ensure_textures_ready()` (bundle only) from visual commit; `on_chunk_manager_ready()` + `chunk_ready` trigger material/position refresh |
| **world_features** | Awaits textures only — no longer blocks on ChunkManager |
| **WorldVisuals / FeatureVisualLayer** | Same texture-only wait; `chunk_ready` → deferred layer refresh |
| **ChunkManager** | `_unload_chunk_view()` uses `remove_child` + `queue_free`; `_exit_tree` calls `release_all_chunks_for_teardown()`; mesh queue cleared + tokens invalidated on teardown |
| **ChunkView** | Explicit child removal before freeing MultiMesh children |
| **PerformanceService** | Single deferred `_apply_to_scene`; skips duplicate preset re-apply from ConfigService |
| **CrystalTextureGenerator** | Registry always uses autoload (fallback is a child node, not orphan) |

